# Config for VS Code's clang language server (clangd) only. It does NOT affect the build —
# Xcode / xcodebuild compile this project with their own flags and report none of these.
#
# When clangd analyzes an Objective-C file on its own, it lacks Xcode's header-search paths
# and builds with modules off. Everything then cascades from headers it can't locate:
#   pp_file_not_found           "'<Header>.h' file not found"  (the header exists; its folder
#                               just isn't on clangd's search path)
#   atimport                    "Use of '@import' when modules are disabled"  (Xcode has them on)
#   unknown_typename / _suggest a type is unknown only because its defining header wasn't found
#   undeclared_protocol         same, for an @protocol
#   objc_property_requires_object  a follow-on: a @property of a type clangd couldn't resolve
#
# These categories are unreliable when a single file is parsed without the real build context,
# so they're suppressed here. Genuine problems still surface in Xcode and in `xcodebuild`.
Diagnostics:
  Suppress:
    - pp_file_not_found
    - atimport
    - unknown_typename
    - unknown_typename_suggest
    - undeclared_protocol
    - objc_property_requires_object
